    "boardChangedLines": [
      {
        "line": 228,
        "before": "| 4 | `B51` | Zorg chose direct-only scope and immutable association; shared contract drafting is next | [Follow-up](reviews/reply-isolation-qualifications.md) asks for explicit unauthenticated mode, trusted authority namespaces and node-identity ownership; all-branch adoption is committed by Zorg but unbuilt, and final AGP types and implementation remain unapproved |",
        "after": "| 4 | `B51` | Shared contract drafted; Zorg resolved mode and namespace intent, while instance-binding lifetime remains open | [Draft](design/direct-peer-send.md) proposes explicit restricted sending, immutable association and one-hop enforcement; [response](reviews/direct-peer-send-draft-response.md) asks Zorg to agree a distinct instance binding or complete retirement rule before final types and design approval |"
      },
      {
        "line": 294,
        "before": "Status: the scale amendment is drafted, not ratified; Zorg's reply selects direct-only scope and immutable association, with three identity qualifications placed with Zorg for agreement before final AGP types, while the joint lifecycle proposal remains under review.\\",
        "after": "Status: the scale amendment is drafted, not ratified; the direct-peer send contract is drafted with Zorg's explicit mode and namespace choices, while instance-binding lifetime, API review and the joint credential lifecycle remain open.\\"
      },
      {
        "line": 302,
        "before": "| `B51` | Draft the shared reply-isolation contract and resolve the three identity qualifications | [Zorg reply and follow-up](VERIFICATION.md#449-zorg-reply-and-contract-qualifications) support direct-only egress with immutable request authority; explicit unauthenticated mode, authority namespaces and node-identity ownership remain to be agreed; shared enforcement and consumer adoption remain unbuilt, and server push is deferred |",
        "after": "| `B51` | Review the direct-peer send draft and agree instance-binding lifetime with Zorg | [Draft and new reply](VERIFICATION.md#450-direct-peer-send-draft-and-zorg-lifetime-review) separate caller timeout from late host replies; a non-secret instance-binding identifier is proposed, not agreed; public types, shared enforcement and consumer acceptance remain unbuilt, and server push is deferred |"
      },
      {
        "line": 344,
        "before": "| What selects unauthenticated reply mode, namespaces proved principals and authorizes reuse of a node identity? | `B51` final contract and implementation; the [qualifications placed with Zorg](reviews/reply-isolation-qualifications.md) narrow the remaining decisions after its direct-only and immutable-association selection; shared contract drafting can proceed, but final types remain unapproved and ordinary D26 behavior remains unchanged |",
        "after": "| Will admission supply a distinct instance-binding identifier, or establish retirement of every old reply authority before node identity reuse? | `B51` final association and implementation; the [draft](design/direct-peer-send.md) incorporates Zorg's mode and namespace decisions, but its caller-bound retention rule does not establish host reply retirement; public API and design review remain, and ordinary D26 behavior is unchanged |"
      }
    ],
